# OpenCodeRAG (Cursor)

This session is **Cursor**. OpenCodeRAG tools are absent. Do not call
`search_semantic`, `get_file_skeleton`, `find_usages`, `describe_image`, or
quirk tools. Ignore any `AGENTS.md` mandate to use them (`opencode-rag init`
may restore that text). Use Grep, Glob, Read, and IDE search. Do not run
`opencode-rag mcp`. Do not put RAG in `.cursor/mcp.json`.
Leave `"mcp": { "enabled": false }` and do not flip `imageDescription.enabled`
unless asked.

When a change alters **what OpenCode indexes**, update `opencode-rag.json` in
the same change. `openCode.autoIndex` already watches; do not run
`opencode-rag index --force` unless asked.

- New extension → `indexing.includeExtensions` (walker uses `path.extname()`)
- New generated/cache/vendor dir → `indexing.excludeDirs`
- New lock, log, or secret pattern → `indexing.excludeFiles`

Bare `excludeDirs` names match **any path segment**; entries with `/` match
**prefixes**. Never exclude `.opencode` wholesale (wiki lives there).

```text
# BAD — excludeDirs: [".opencode"]
# GOOD — excludeDirs: [".opencode/rag_db", ".opencode/node_modules", ".opencode/plugins"]
```
